# Antigravity (Gemini) kit — environment variables for skill scripts
# Setup: copy this file to .gemini/.env and fill in the values. Never commit .gemini/.env
#
# Resolution order (highest to lowest):
#   1. process.env                         runtime
#   2. .gemini/skills/<skill>/.env          per-skill override
#   3. .gemini/skills/.env                  shared by all skills
#   4. .gemini/.env                         project-wide default (this file)
#   5-7. the same three under ~/.gemini/config/ (user-wide)
#
# Debug: python3 .gemini/scripts/resolve_env.py --show-hierarchy
#
# Note: Antigravity itself signs in with your Google account. GEMINI_API_KEY below is only for
# the skill scripts that call the Gemini API directly (ck-ai-multimodal, ck-research).

# ============================================
# Google Gemini API — skills: ck-ai-multimodal, ck-research
# ============================================
# Get a key at https://aistudio.google.com/apikey
GEMINI_API_KEY=

# Optional — rotate across several keys when rate limited
# (see .gemini/skills/common/api_key_rotator.py)
# GEMINI_API_KEY_2=
# GEMINI_API_KEY_3=

# Optional — model overrides
# GEMINI_MODEL=
# GEMINI_IMAGE_GEN_MODEL=

# Optional — use Vertex AI instead of AI Studio
# GEMINI_USE_VERTEX=true
# VERTEX_PROJECT_ID=
# VERTEX_LOCATION=us-central1

# ============================================
# Context7 — skill: ck-docs-seeker, and the context7 MCP server
# ============================================
# Get a key at https://context7.com/dashboard/api-keys
# CONTEXT7_API_KEY=

# ============================================
# MCP servers
# ============================================
# Antigravity reads MCP servers from ~/.gemini/config/mcp_config.json (global) — there is no
# per-project file. Merge .gemini/mcp_config.json.example into it, or add each server with
#   agy mcp add <name> <command> [args...]
# then check: agy mcp list   (or … > MCP Servers in the app)
#
# The template covers the servers these skills need:
#   gitnexus             AGENTS.md + the gitnexus-* skills
#   pencil               required by ui-design-pencil (71 references)
#   sequential-thinking  backs the ck-sequential-thinking skill
#   context7             docs lookup; paste CONTEXT7_API_KEY into its --api-key arg
#
# pencil: the path is a local macOS arm64 app binary (/Applications/Pen.app/...). Read the correct
# path from your Pencil install. Its --agent value was claudeCodeCLI in the Claude kit; the
# "antigravity" value in the template is unverified — check the binary's --help.
